<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
<meta charset="utf-8">
<title>RangeWatch bulletin — {{ species.scientific_name }} (v{{ mv.model_version }})</title>
<link rel="stylesheet" href="bulletin.css">
</head>
<body>

<!-- 1. Header -->
<header class="masthead">
  <div class="masthead-text">
    <p class="kicker">RangeWatch · Species distribution bulletin</p>
    <h1><em>{{ species.scientific_name }}</em></h1>
    {% if species.common_name %}<p class="common">{{ species.common_name }}</p>{% endif %}
    <p class="meta">
      GBIF taxon key {{ species.taxon_key }} · Model v{{ mv.model_version }}
      ({{ "Model B — native + invaded" if mv.model_type == "B" else "Model A — native only" }})
      · Generated {{ generated }}
    </p>
    <p class="meta">Occurrence data: {{ repro.gbif_citation }}</p>
    {% if repro.inat_citation %}<p class="meta">Supplementary data: {{ repro.inat_citation }}</p>{% endif %}
  </div>
  {% if species.thumbnail_url %}
  <img class="thumb" src="{{ species.thumbnail_url }}" alt="">
  {% endif %}
</header>

{% if mv.model_type == "A" %}
<div class="banner warn">
  <strong>Lower-confidence projection.</strong> No documented introduced-range records were
  available, so this model was trained on native-range data only (Model A).
</div>
{% endif %}

<!-- 2. Executive summary -->
<section>
  <h2>Executive summary</h2>
  <p class="lead">{{ summary }}</p>
  <div class="caveat"><strong>Transferability caveat.</strong> {{ caveat }}</div>
</section>

<!-- 3. Map panel 1 -->
<section class="figure">
  <h2>Native range and suitability</h2>
  <img src="{{ figures.native_map }}" alt="Native-range occurrence map">
  <p class="caption">Occurrences by effective range label over continuous suitability; white
    contour = binarisation threshold ({{ m.threshold | num(3) }}, {{ m.threshold_rule }});
    dashed line = native-range polygon, {{ native_status }}.</p>
</section>

<!-- 4. Map panel 2 -->
<section class="figure">
  <h2>Global projection, candidate invasion zones and extrapolation</h2>
  <img src="{{ figures.global_map }}" alt="Global projection map">
  <p class="caption">Hatched cells have MESS &lt; 0: at least one predictor lies outside the
    training range, so suitability there is an extrapolation and should be treated with low
    confidence. {{ m.projection.extrapolation_area_km2 | num }} km² of land is extrapolated.</p>
</section>

{% if extrapolation %}
<!-- 4b. Advanced extrapolation diagnostics -->
<section class="figure">
  <h2>Extrapolation diagnostics</h2>
  {% if figures.consensus_map %}<img src="{{ figures.consensus_map }}" alt="Extrapolation consensus map">{% endif %}
  <p class="caption">Number of the five diagnostics that flag each land cell as extrapolation.
    They test different things: MESS and exDet NT1 check predictor ranges, exDet NT2 detects
    novel combinations of in-range values, MOP and Shape measure distance to the closest
    analogous training conditions, and AOA measures distance in the importance-weighted
    predictor space the model relies on. Where several agree, suitability is least reliable.
    {{ (extrapolation.candidate_consensus_ok_fraction * 100) | num }}% of the candidate zone is
    flagged by none and {{ (extrapolation.candidate_consensus_majority_fraction * 100) | num }}%
    by at least three.</p>
  <table class="compact">
    <tr><th>Diagnostic</th><th>Flags extrapolation when</th><th>Threshold</th>
        <th>Land flagged</th><th>Candidate zone flagged</th></tr>
    {% for d in extrapolation.diagnostics %}
    <tr><td>{{ d.label }} <span class="small">({{ d.reference }})</span></td>
        <td>{{ d.flag_rule }}</td>
        <td>{{ d.threshold | num(3) }}</td>
        <td>{{ (d.land_fraction * 100) | num(1) }}%</td>
        <td>{{ (d.candidate_flagged_fraction * 100) | num(1) }}%</td></tr>
    {% endfor %}
  </table>
  <p class="small">Reference set: {{ extrapolation.reference_set }}
    (n = {{ extrapolation.n_reference | num }}). exDet uses its published cut-offs (NT1 &lt; 0,
    NT2 &gt; 1). MOP (mean distance to the closest {{ extrapolation.mop_percentage }}% of
    reference points, z-scored), Shape and AOA (importance-weighted) thresholds are the
    outlier-trimmed maximum, min(Q75 + 1.5·IQR, max), of the training points' values against
    the other {{ extrapolation.n_cv_folds - 1 }} spatial CV folds (Meyer &amp; Pebesma 2021).
    {% if extrapolation.combinatorial %}Novel combinations (exDet NT2 &gt; 1,
    {{ extrapolation.exdet_combinatorial_area_km2 | num }} km²) are driven mainly by
    {% for d in extrapolation.combinatorial %}{{ d.name }}{% if not loop.last %}, {% endif %}{% endfor %}.{% endif %}</p>
</section>
{% endif %}

<div class="two-col">
  <!-- 5. Severity gauge -->
  <section>
    <h2>Severity index</h2>
    {% if figures.gauge %}<img src="{{ figures.gauge }}" alt="Severity gauge">{% endif %}
    <table class="compact">
      <tr><th>Component</th><th>S</th><th>w</th><th>w·S</th></tr>
      {# fixed order: jsonb does not preserve key order #}
      {% for k in severity_components %}{% set v = sev.components[k] %}
      <tr><td>{{ k.replace('_', ' ') }}</td><td>{{ v | num(2) }}</td>
          <td>{{ sev.weights[k] | num(2) }}</td><td>{{ sev.contributions[k] | num(3) }}</td></tr>
      {% endfor %}
      <tr class="total"><td>Severity</td><td></td><td></td><td>{{ sev.score | num(3) }}</td></tr>
    </table>
    <p class="small">Confidence: <strong>{{ sev.confidence.level }}</strong>
      ({% if sev.confidence.basis == "consensus" %}{{ (sev.confidence.consensus_majority_fraction * 100) | num }}%
      of candidate area flagged by ≥ 3 of 5 extrapolation diagnostics,
      {{ (sev.confidence.consensus_ok_fraction * 100) | num }}% by none; {% endif %}{{ (sev.confidence.mess_ok_fraction * 100) | num }}%
      with MESS ≥ 0. {{ sev.confidence.note }})
      {% if sev.confidence.reasons %}Lowered by: {{ sev.confidence.reasons | join('; ') }}.{% endif %}</p>
  </section>

  <!-- 6. Variable importance -->
  <section>
    <h2>Variable importance</h2>
    <img src="{{ figures.importance }}" alt="Variable importance">
    <ul class="small">
      {% for p in m.predictors %}<li>{{ p.upper() }} — {{ bioclim_names[p] }}</li>{% endfor %}
    </ul>
  </section>
</div>

<!-- 7. Diagnostics -->
<section>
  <h2>Model diagnostics</h2>
  <table>
    <tr><th>Metric</th><th>Value</th><th>Metric</th><th>Value</th></tr>
    <tr><td>AUC (spatial CV)</td><td>{{ m.auc_mean | num(3) }} ± {{ m.auc_std | num(3) }}</td>
        <td>n presences (thinned)</td><td>{{ m.n_presence | num }}</td></tr>
    <tr><td>CBI (spatial CV)</td><td>{{ m.cbi_mean | num(3) }} ± {{ m.cbi_std | num(3) }}</td>
        <td>n background</td><td>{{ m.n_background | num }} ({{ m.background_method }})</td></tr>
    <tr><td>TSS (spatial CV)</td><td>{{ m.tss_mean | num(3) }} ± {{ m.tss_std | num(3) }}</td>
        <td>CV folds</td><td>{{ m.n_cv_folds }} — {{ m.cv_method }}</td></tr>
    <tr><td>Training AUC</td><td>{{ m.train_auc | num(3) }}</td>
        <td>Features / regularisation</td><td>{{ m.feature_classes }} / β = {{ m.beta_multiplier }}</td></tr>
  </table>
</section>

<!-- 8. Expansion outlook -->
<section>
  <h2>Expansion outlook</h2>
  <img src="{{ figures.timeline }}" alt="Records per year">
  <p>{{ outlook.trend }}
    {% if outlook.spread_rate is not none %}Newly occupied 1° cells outside the native range:
    {{ outlook.spread_rate | num(1) }} per year.{% endif %}</p>
  {% if outlook.regions %}
  <p><strong>Largest candidate invasion zones (10° tiles):</strong>
    {% for r in outlook.regions %}{{ r.tile }} ({{ r.area_km2 | num }} km²){% if not loop.last %}; {% endif %}{% endfor %}.</p>
  {% endif %}
  {% if outlook.limiting %}
  <p><strong>Main sources of extrapolation (MESS most-dissimilar variable):</strong>
    {% for d in outlook.limiting %}{{ d.name }}{% if not loop.last %}, {% endif %}{% endfor %}.</p>
  {% endif %}
  <div class="caveat">{{ caveat }}</div>
</section>

<!-- 9. Methods & references -->
<section class="methods">
  <h2>Methods &amp; reproducibility</h2>
  <p>Presence-background MaxEnt (elapid {{ repro.package_versions.elapid }}) with feature
    classes and regularisation selected from the Wallace/ENMeval default grid by spatially
    block-cross-validated CBI. Occurrences were cleaned, de-duplicated to one per raster cell
    and distance-thinned ({{ repro.training_config.thin_km }} km);
    {% set bgi = repro.background %}
    {% if bgi and bgi.target_group and not bgi.fallback_reason %}
    background points were drawn from raster cells holding GBIF records of the target group
    ({{ bgi.target_group.rank }} {{ bgi.target_group.name }},
    {{ bgi.target_group.n_records | num }} records) within a
    {{ repro.training_config.background_buffer_km | num }} km buffer of presences, so that the
    background shares the observer bias of the presences (target-group background).
    {% else %}
    background points were sampled uniformly within a
    {{ repro.training_config.background_buffer_km | num }} km buffer of presences{% if bgi and bgi.fallback_reason %}
    (target-group background not used: {{ bgi.fallback_reason }}){% endif %}.
    {% endif %}
    Predictors: {{ m.predictors | join(', ') | upper }} (global VIF &lt; 5 screen of
    {{ repro.bioclim_version_used }}, {{ repro.bioclim_source }}). Native-range polygon:
    {{ native_status }}.</p>
  <p><strong>Severity index.</strong> {{ severity_footnote }}</p>
  <table class="compact">
    <tr><td>Bioclim version</td><td>{{ repro.bioclim_version_used }} (sha256 {{ (repro.bioclim_sha256 or 'n/a')[:12] }})</td></tr>
    <tr><td>GBIF download</td><td>{{ repro.gbif_download_doi or repro.gbif_download_key or 'search API (no DOI)' }}</td></tr>
    <tr><td>Packages</td><td>{% for k, v in repro.package_versions.items() %}{{ k }} {{ v }}{% if not loop.last %}, {% endif %}{% endfor %}</td></tr>
    <tr><td>Random seeds</td><td>{% for k, v in repro.random_seeds.items() %}{{ k }}={{ v }}{% if not loop.last %}, {% endif %}{% endfor %}</td></tr>
    <tr><td>MLflow run</td><td>{{ mv.mlflow_run_id or 'n/a' }}</td></tr>
  </table>
  <h3>References</h3>
  <ol class="refs">
    {% for r in references %}<li>{{ r }}</li>{% endfor %}
  </ol>
</section>

</body>
</html>
